      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{618ece8f22b63e309408b761|full_name} I agree about the networking problems and also think there should be hard limitations to it. It does not have to be on the same scale as the avatar or world. Maybe adding a spawn limit like they did with prints. So if world creators want to disable it to avoid problems in the future, maybe it should be an option?\n\nUnfortunately for avatars and world creators, inevitable things can happen regardless of their wish.\n\nThis would kind of support in reducing the performance stats on avatars. Although you may have some things toggled off, the performance stats don't change. So that's why we should keep props separated as it just becomes a different performance ranking that can be spawned or removed from the world instance at any time.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
